config VIDEO_MEDIATEK_VCODEC_MT8167
	tristate "Mediatek Video Codec driver for MT8365/MT8167 SoC (vendor, Genio 350)"
	depends on MTK_IOMMU || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on VIDEO_DEV
	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on VIDEO_MEDIATEK_VCU_MT8365
	select VIDEOBUF2_DMA_CONTIG
	select V4L2_MEM2MEM_DEV
	default n
	help
	    Vendor MT8365/MT8167 (Genio 350) video codec driver ported from
	    the mtk-v5.10 BSP. Provides HW encode/decode of a range of video
	    formats via the proprietary userspace (vpud) path; relies on the
	    VCU (CONFIG_VIDEO_MEDIATEK_VCU_MT8365) to talk to the codec engine.

	    This depends on the vendor VCU rather than mainline's
	    CONFIG_VIDEO_MEDIATEK_VPU. The original BSP "depends on
	    !VIDEO_MEDIATEK_VCODEC" guard is dropped: the vendor modules use a
	    distinct module name (mtk-vcodec-mt8167-dec/-enc/-common) and do
	    not bind the same DT compatibles as mainline's mtk-vcodec.

	    To compile this driver as modules, choose M here: the modules will
	    be called mtk-vcodec-mt8167-dec, mtk-vcodec-mt8167-enc and
	    mtk-vcodec-mt8167-common.
